@extends('layouts.app')

@section('content')
<div class="container docs-shell">
    @include('partials.docs-side')
    <article class="docs-body">
        <h1>Queues</h1>
        <p>Jobs implement <code class="inline">Job</code> and expose <code class="inline">handle()</code>. The <code class="inline">sync</code> driver runs work immediately. The <code class="inline">array</code> driver stores jobs in memory until <code class="inline">queue:work</code>.</p>

        <pre><code>class WelcomeMail(val email: String) : Job {
    override fun handle() {
        Mail.send(email, "Welcome", "&lt;p&gt;Hi&lt;/p&gt;")
    }
}

dispatch(WelcomeMail("ada@example.com"))
Queue.push(WelcomeMail("ada@example.com"))</code></pre>
        <pre><code>./gradlew run --args='queue:work --once'</code></pre>
        <p>There is no Redis/database worker and no delayed retry backend. <code class="inline">later(seconds, job)</code> is honored by the array driver; sync still runs immediately.</p>
    </article>
</div>
@endsection
